{"repositoryId":664935518,"availability":"available","full":"rexfordessilfie/next-auth-express-demo","name":"next-auth-express-demo","description":"Using NextAuth in an Express Backend","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2023-07-11T04:46:23Z","updated":"2023-07-11T22:14:33Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://next-auth-express-demo.onrender.com","topics":["express","nextauth","nextjs"],"demo":"https://next-auth-express-demo.onrender.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:41.564Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:41.564Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:41.564Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T23:48:41.564Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This demo show-cases an approach to using NextAuth in an Express backend.","The Next.js Pages Router and Express Framework extend the same Request and Response interfaces with additional some common functionality. While the compatibility is not 1:1, it is enough such that next-auth (v4) is cross-compatible.","For example, methods such as res.send(), and res.json() are implemented across both response types. However methods such as res.revalidate() exist in Next.js land only. This is okay since the method is not used in NextAuth (v4)."],"features":["Making sure we apply some middleware functions (Step 2) in order to parse and fill some request object properties in Express.","Manually parsing the request path into the Catch-all Dynamic Segments as is done automatically in Next.js. This is specifically relied on by NextAuth."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rexfordessilfie/next-auth-express-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7df3aaac4d5bdd9135ba1696abb5bd3ed5425edb8403f25518380df7a6ca3374","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:41.653Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T23:48:41.653Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This demo show-cases an app